tant"},{"id":"D","text":"the survey results"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Link the opening participle clause to the **subject of the main clause**.","explanation":"The introductory participle clause normally shares its understood subject with **the assistant**, the main-clause subject.","keywords":["shared-participle-subject"],"skill":"shared-participle-subject","contextKey":"participle-clauses-48","fingerprint":"b6d9ca9be922aea4cfdbebb44601466f2b7aae509abeff1b5ae9a91135f92fba","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-participles"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Link the opening participle clause to the **subject of the main clause**.","The introductory participle clause normally shares its understood subject with **the assistant**, the main-clause subject.","Choose **the assistant**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The structure normally links the implied actor to the main-clause subject.","B":"The main subject supplies the understood actor in this construction.","C":"The introductory participle clause normally shares its understood subject with **the assistant**, the main-clause subject.","D":"This is the object of the earlier action, not the actor."}}},{"id":"fa91c35d-5644-5afa-a39c-c0c90ffb1299","topicSlug":"participle-clauses","level":"C1","prompt":"Add an active participle clause: “____ the evening meal, the assistant noticed a mistake.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Has prepared"},{"id":"B","text":"preparing"},{"id":"C","text":"To prepare"},{"id":"D","text":"prepares"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The assistant performs both actions, so an **active -ing clause** can share that subject.","explanation":"**preparing the evening meal** describes the assistant’s activity; the main subject supplies the understood actor.","keywords":["active-participle"],"skill":"active-participl